875
00:28:22,866 --> 00:28:23,748
Question one.

876
00:28:23,928 --> 00:28:25,704
Aren't old cars unsafe?

877
00:28:25,884 --> 00:28:28,081
Safety has improved a lot over the

878
00:28:28,081 --> 00:28:30,665
years, so it's worth checking crash test

879
00:28:30,665 --> 00:28:33,766
ratings from the Insurance Institute for Highway

880
00:28:33,766 --> 00:28:36,609
Safety and the government's NHTSA before you

881
00:28:36,609 --> 00:28:36,867
buy.

882
00:28:37,047 --> 00:28:38,611
But many cars that are a few

883
00:28:38,611 --> 00:28:40,902
years old have excellent safety features.

884
00:28:41,082 --> 00:28:43,721
Driving a modest car doesn't mean driving

885
00:28:43,721 --> 00:28:44,623
an unsafe one.

886
00:28:44,973 --> 00:28:45,843
Question two.

887
00:28:46,023 --> 00:28:47,995
Don't repairs on an old car cost

888
00:28:47,995 --> 00:28:49,228
more than a payment?

889
00:28:49,408 --> 00:28:51,346
Sometimes, but often not.

890
00:28:51,526 --> 00:28:53,849
Even a major repair costing a couple

891
00:28:53,849 --> 00:28:56,495
thousand dollars is usually far less than

892
00:28:56,495 --> 00:28:58,237
a year of new car payments.

893
00:28:58,417 --> 00:29:00,436
The key is to budget for repairs

894
00:29:00,436 --> 00:29:02,140
in advance with a car fund,

895
00:29:02,140 --> 00:29:04,222
so they don't become emergencies.

896
00:29:04,572 --> 00:29:05,593
Question three.

897
00:29:05,773 --> 00:29:07,515
What about electric cars?

898
00:29:07,695 --> 00:29:10,218
Many electric cars cost less to fuel

899
00:29:10,218 --> 00:29:12,882
and maintain, which can help the total

900
00:29:12,882 --> 00:29:13,233
cost.

901
00:29:13,413 --> 00:29:15,375
The same rules still apply.

902
00:29:15,555 --> 00:29:16,911
Consider buying used,

903
00:29:16,911 --> 00:29:19,558
check the battery warranty and condition,

904
00:29:19,558 --> 00:29:20,849
keep it a long time,

905
00:29:20,849 --> 00:29:23,496
and calculate the full cost of ownership.

906
00:29:23,846 --> 00:29:24,751
Question four.

907
00:29:24,931 --> 00:29:26,847
Can I ever buy my dream car?

908
00:29:27,027 --> 00:29:27,828
Absolutely.

909
00:29:28,008 --> 00:29:29,019
If you love cars,

910
00:29:29,019 --> 00:29:30,921
it can be part of your conscious

911
00:29:30,921 --> 00:29:31,456
spending.

912
00:29:31,636 --> 00:29:33,786
The millionaire way is to buy it

913
00:29:33,786 --> 00:29:36,675
after you've built a strong financial base,

914
00:29:36,675 --> 00:29:38,825
pay cash or keep the loan short,

915
00:29:38,825 --> 00:29:41,243
and cut costs elsewhere to make room

916
00:29:41,243 --> 00:29:41,713
for it.

917
00:29:42,064 --> 00:29:43,108
Question five.

918
00:29:43,288 --> 00:29:45,158
What if I need a reliable car

919
00:29:45,158 --> 00:29:45,738
for work?

920
00:29:45,918 --> 00:29:48,688
Then reliability is exactly what you should

921
00:29:48,688 --> 00:29:49,204
pay for.

922
00:29:49,384 --> 00:29:52,501
Choose models with strong reliability ratings,

923
00:29:52,501 --> 00:29:55,211
have a trusted mechanic inspect any used

924
00:29:55,211 --> 00:29:56,431
car before buying,

925
00:29:56,431 --> 00:29:58,531
and keep an emergency fund so a

926
00:29:58,531 --> 00:30:00,971
breakdown doesn't threaten your job.

927
00:30:01,321 --> 00:30:02,447
Question six.

928
00:30:02,627 --> 00:30:04,078
Should I lease or buy?

929
00:30:04,258 --> 00:30:06,612
For most people who want to minimize

930
00:30:06,612 --> 00:30:07,854
lifetime car costs,

931
00:30:07,854 --> 00:30:10,207
buying a reliable car and keeping it

932
00:30:10,207 --> 00:30:12,430
for many years tends to be cheaper

933
00:30:12,430 --> 00:30:14,719
than leasing one car after another.

934
00:30:14,899 --> 00:30:17,453
Leasing can make sense for some business

935
00:30:17,453 --> 00:30:19,688
owners or people who drive very few

936
00:30:19,688 --> 00:30:21,603
miles and want a new car every

937
00:30:21,603 --> 00:30:23,838
few years, but it means a permanent

938
00:30:23,838 --> 00:30:24,349
payment.

939
00:30:24,529 --> 00:30:26,644
Read every lease term carefully,

940
00:30:26,644 --> 00:30:29,487
especially mileage limits and wear charges.

941
00:30:29,837 --> 00:30:30,870
Question seven.

942
00:30:31,050 --> 00:30:32,423
How do I start a car fund

943
00:30:32,423 --> 00:30:33,906
if I still have a car loan?

944
00:30:34,086 --> 00:30:35,252
Start small now,

945
00:30:35,252 --> 00:30:37,219
even fifty dollars a month,

946
00:30:37,219 --> 00:30:39,113
while you finish the loan.

947
00:30:39,293 --> 00:30:40,992
When the loan is paid off,

948
00:30:40,992 --> 00:30:43,018
add the full old payment to the

949
00:30:43,018 --> 00:30:43,345
fund.

950
00:30:43,525 --> 00:30:44,392
In a few years,

951
00:30:44,392 --> 00:30:46,416
you'll have enough to buy your next

952
00:30:46,416 --> 00:30:47,110
car in cash,

953
00:30:47,110 --> 00:30:48,960
and you'll never need a car loan

954
00:30:48,960 --> 00:30:49,307
again.

955
00:30:49,487 --> 00:30:51,408
That one cycle change can save you

956
00:30:51,408 --> 00:30:53,724
thousands in interest over your lifetime.

957
00:30:54,075 --> 00:30:54,876
Quick recap.

958
00:30:55,056 --> 00:30:56,727
Angle one, the numbers.

959
00:30:56,907 --> 00:30:59,772
Let someone else pay the depreciation,

960
00:30:59,772 --> 00:31:01,732
keep it ten years or more,

961
00:31:01,732 --> 00:31:03,164
know the full cost,

962
00:31:03,164 --> 00:31:05,350
pay cash or keep loans short,

963
00:31:05,350 --> 00:31:07,310
and invest the difference.

964
00:31:07,660 --> 00:31:09,738
Angle two, the psychology.

965
00:31:09,918 --> 00:31:12,094
A car is transportation,

966
00:31:12,094 --> 00:31:13,273
not identity.

967
00:31:13,453 --> 00:31:15,369
Nobody is watching as much as you

968
00:31:15,369 --> 00:31:15,717
think.

969
00:31:15,897 --> 00:31:17,894
Wealth is what you don't see.

970
00:31:18,074 --> 00:31:19,537
Delay gratification.

971
00:31:19,717 --> 00:31:21,447
And escape the hedonic treadmill.

972
00:31:21,797 --> 00:31:23,457
Angle three, the playbook.

973
00:31:23,637 --> 00:31:25,593
Maintenance beats replacement,

974
00:31:25,593 --> 00:31:27,746
borrow only for things that grow,

975
00:31:27,746 --> 00:31:30,355
insure smart, automate the good choices,

976
00:31:30,355 --> 00:31:32,311
and spend big on what you love

977
00:31:32,311 --> 00:31:34,724
while cutting ruthlessly on the rest.

978
00:31:35,075 --> 00:31:37,478
Here's the big idea one more time.

979
00:31:37,658 --> 00:31:39,525
A car is one of the largest

980
00:31:39,525 --> 00:31:41,392
purchases most people make,

981
00:31:41,392 --> 00:31:42,360
over and over,

982
00:31:42,360 --> 00:31:43,950
for their entire lives.

983
00:31:44,130 --> 00:31:46,113
Getting that one decision right,

984
00:31:46,113 --> 00:31:47,104
again and again,

985
00:31:47,104 --> 00:31:49,149
can be worth more than almost any

986
00:31:49,149 --> 00:31:51,131
investment tip you'll ever hear.

987
00:31:51,311 --> 00:31:53,519
Buy reliable, buy slightly used,

988
00:31:53,519 --> 00:31:54,417
keep it long,

989
00:31:54,417 --> 00:31:56,211
and invest the difference.

990
00:31:56,391 --> 00:31:57,996
So next time you see an old

991
00:31:57,996 --> 00:31:59,601
car in a nice neighborhood,

992
00:31:59,601 --> 00:32:01,801
don't assume the owner is struggling.

993
00:32:01,981 --> 00:32:03,677
They might be the richest person on

994
00:32:03,677 --> 00:32:04,210
the street.

995
00:32:04,390 --> 00:32:06,031
If you want the full plan for

996
00:32:06,031 --> 00:32:08,011
